  "configuration_id": "config_046",
  "reason": "The current best (config_043: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.725 acc. The single most important untested design variable is the RNA encoder in the multiprofile/transformer setting, since all completed multiprofile experiments used scvi_n200. config_046 swaps only the RNA encoder to pca_n2000 while holding image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (transformer), fusion (weighted), and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. This isolates whether a learned nonlinear representation (scvi) is meaningfully better than a linear PCA projection for the RNA modality when profiles are aggregated by a transformer. If pca_n2000 performs comparably, the RNA encoder is not a bottleneck and we can redirect budget to other variables (e.g., image encoder or fusion); if it degrades substantially, scvi's learned representation is confirmed as critical. This single-variable comparison from the current best is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

